  "query_preview": "..A benign weather pattern for this week across \nsoutheast Arizona. In the near term, shortwave ridging aloft \ncontinues to build into the region from the west. Still considerable \nmoisture levels at the immediate surface and this may lead to some \npatchy fog this morning in the normally susceptible locations east \nof Tucson such as the Sulphur Springs Valley. Any fog will quickly \nburn off this morning with abundant sunshine thereafter for the \nentire forecast area and daytime highs about 5 to 8 degrees below \nnormal. \n\nA couple of weak systems will pass well to our north Wednesday and \nThursday with dry westerly flow dominating our weather with just \nsome high clouds from time to time. Thereafter, the flow pattern \nbecomes more dominated by broad baggy troughing Friday into the \nweekend over our forecast area. There are some differences in the \nexact evolution of this pattern in the ensembles by Sunday/Monday \nwith the GEFS showing more established troughing to our southwest \nalong the Baja peninsula while the EPS/GEPS are much more muted with \nany troughing. Will maintain dry forecast through this period as \ntemperatures remain about 5 degrees below normal.",
